---
/**
 * Dark, always.
 *
 * Starlight has no `defaultTheme` option — its own ThemeProvider reads
 * `localStorage['starlight-theme']`, falls back to `prefers-color-scheme`, and
 * stamps `data-theme` accordingly. The rest of unityide.app has no light mode
 * and no theme toggle, so a visitor whose OS prefers light was the one person
 * getting a page the site cannot actually paint.
 *
 * `starlight-overrides.css` declares its tokens under all three `data-theme`
 * states as a second line of defence, but this is the one that makes
 * "dark-only" true rather than merely survivable.
 *
 * `window.StarlightThemeProvider` is kept because Starlight's ThemeSelect calls
 * `updatePickers()` on it. That picker is hidden here, but a missing global
 * would throw on any page that still mounts one.
 */
---

{/* Inlined, like Starlight's own, so there is no flash before it runs. */}
<script is:inline>
  document.documentElement.dataset.theme = 'dark';
  window.StarlightThemeProvider = { updatePickers() {} };
</script>
